pears before WORK EXPERIENCE. Toggling skills.visible to false removed the SKILLS block and its content from the preview; toggling back restored it.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggle labeled \\\"Hide Preview\\\" removed editor.preview/preview.document from the DOM and became \\\"Show Preview\\\"; clicking again restored the preview with the same Classic-style rendering (\\\"Jane Tester / jane@example.com / • 555-0100 ...\\\") and editor content intact (experience company still \\\"Acme Corp\\\").\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Card menu → Duplicate created \\\"QA Lead Application (Copy)\\\" (id f50os8qr4h) alongside the source. Renamed it via the Rename dialog to \\\"Automation Architect Application\\\". Opened the copy: it carried the source content, and editing it (full-name→\\\"Jane T. Architect\\\", email→arch@example.com, company→\\\"Copy Corp\\\") left the source \\\"QA Lead Application\\\" unchanged (Jane Tester / jane@example.com / Acme Corp).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Session now holds 6 coexisting resumes including 3 created this session: \\\"QA Lead Application\\\" (Classic, Jane Tester/Acme Corp), \\\"Automation Architect Application\\\" (Classic, Jane T. Architect/Copy Corp, a renamed duplicate) and \\\"Zeta Startup Pitch Resume\\\" (Modern, Zed Founder). Each opens with its own independent content and template.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"RESUME\\\" (uppercase) matched the 4 lowercase-\\\"Resume\\\" titles and excluded the 2 \\\"...Application\\\" ones; \\\"qa lead\\\" (lowercase) matched only \\\"QA Lead Application\\\" — case-insensitive both ways. Clearing the box restored all 6 resumes. Sort \\\"Newest First\\\" listed Zeta / Automation Architect / QA Lead / Product Designer / Marketing Manager / Software Engineer; \\\"Oldest First\\\" produced the exact reverse (Software Engineer Jan 20 2024 → Marketing Feb 10 → Product Designer Feb 25 → QA Lead → Copy → Zeta), matching creation order.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Date filtering feature is entirely absent from the dashboard\", \"actual\": \"The dashboard toolbar contains only a text search box (dashboard.search) and a sort dropdown (dashboard.sort with newest/oldest/title-asc/title-desc). A DOM scan found 0 input[type=date] elements and no date-range or exact-date controls anywhere on the page, so saved resumes cannot be narrowed by creation date.\", \"evidence\": \"Full DOM control inventory of dashboard: submit \\\"New Resume\\\", text \\\"Search resumes...\\\", button \\\"Newest First\\\", 3 card menu buttons. dateInputs: 0\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date-period validation on experience/education entries\", \"actual\": \"Set Acme Corp experience start=2020-01 with end=2019-05 (end before start): no error, no styling change, item text unchanged (\\\"Position 1 / Company / Position / Start Date / End Date...\\\"), no message anywhere in body. Then set start=2030-01 (future, today is 2026-08-28): also accepted. The preview rendered the invalid period verbatim as \\\"Jan 2030 - May 2019\\\". Date inputs are type=month with no max attribute.\", \"evidence\": \"preview.document text: \\\"Senior QA Engineer / Acme Corp / Jan 2030 - May 2019\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All experience and education date inputs are input[type=month]; preview renders \\\"Mon YYYY\\\" consistently (\\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\", \\\"Mar 2017 - Dec 2019\\\", \\\"Sep 2013 - May 2017\\\"). Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" cleared end-date value to \\\"\\\" and set disabled=true; preview switched that entry to \\\"- Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all resume changes are lost on reload and deletions are resurrected\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard held 5 resumes: created \\\"QA Lead Application\\\" (edited, renamed from Untitled), duplicated+renamed \\\"Automation Architect Application\\\", created \\\"Zeta Startup Pitch Resume\\\", plus seeds resume-3 and resume-1 (\\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\" had been deleted via the confirm dialog). After navigating to http://localhost:7005/ again, the dashboard reverted to the 3 original seed resumes: Product Designer Resume, Marketing Manager Resume (the deleted one is back), Software Engineer Resume. All 3 session resumes and every content edit were lost. localStorage and sessionStorage are both empty, so state is in-memory only.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload dashboard.resumes items: [resume-3 Product Designer, resume-2 Marketing Manager, resume-1 Software Engineer]; localStorageKeys=[], sessionStorageKeys=[]\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Dashboard rename dialog accepts a whitespace-only title (resume left with a blank name); editor rename silently reverts with no feedback\", \"actual\": \"Path A (dashboard menu → Rename dialog): entered \\\"   \\\" and clicked Save. The dialog closed, the rename was APPLIED and the card title became an empty string (semantic_observe of dashboard.resumes.item.f50os8qr4h returns name:\\\"\\\"). No validation message shown. Path B (editor header title): entering \\\"   \\\" or \\\"\\\" and pressing Enter reverts to the previous title but shows no message at all — sonner toaster empty, no [role=alert]/[aria-live] text, no inline error.\", \"evidence\": \"After Save with whitespace: dialogOpen=false, card innerText=\\\"\\\", toaster=\\\"none\\\"\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"No save button exists; every edit propagated to preview.document on the spot: contact fields (Jane Tester/jane@example.com/...) appeared immediately after fill, summary text, experience/education entries, skill add+level change+removal, and template switches Modern→Classic→Minimal→Modern each re-rendered the preview instantly without refresh.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"education.move-up and skills.visible toggles each re-rendered preview.document instantly (EDUCATION moved above WORK EXPERIENCE; SKILLS block disappeared/reappeared). After navigating across editor tabs, out to the dashboard and back into the resume, the preview still shows ACADEMIC BACKGROUND before CAREER HISTORY with SKILLS visible, so the custom layout survived in-session navigation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"No manual save exists; all edits made across the Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections tabs were intact after editor.back to the dashboard and reopening the card. The dashboard card showed the refreshed stamp \\\"Updated Aug 28, 2026\\\" (today) and template \\\"Classic\\\" matching the chosen style.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"In each style (Modern/Classic/Minimal) the preview rendered content for all 5 visible sections (contact, summary, experience x2, education, skills). After enlarging content (497-char summary + ~700-char description) the preview region grew from 741px to 1077px, preview.document was fully laid out (height 720px, bottom 444px inside preview bottom 777px, nothing clipped) and the page became scrollable (documentElement scrollHeight 1187 vs clientHeight 720), with the last line \\\"CORE COMPETENCIES / Playwright • TypeScript\\\" present.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching across all 7 editor tabs, returning to dashboard via editor.back and reopening the card, the editor/preview still contained: contact (Jane Tester, jane@example.com, 555-0100, Boston MA, linkedin.com/in/janetester, janetester.dev), the full 497-char summary, both experience entries (Senior QA Engineer/Acme Corp/Jan 2020–Present and QA Analyst/Beta Inc/Mar 2017–Dec 2019 with long description), education (State University, BSc Computer Science, GPA 3.8, Sep 2013–May 2017) and skills (Playwright • TypeScript).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Copy→original isolation: after editing the copy (name \\\"Jane T. Architect\\\", email arch@example.com, company \\\"Copy Corp\\\"), the original still read Jane Tester / jane@example.com / Acme Corp, Beta Inc. Original→copy isolation: after editing the original (location→\\\"Cambridge, MA\\\", added skill \\\"OriginalOnlySkill\\\"), the copy still read location \\\"Boston, MA\\\", skills \\\"Playwright • TypeScript\\\" with no OriginalOnlySkill, and companies Copy Corp / Beta Inc. Both directions isolated despite the copy reusing the same nested entry ids.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed to \\\"QA Lead Application\\\"; editor.title reads \\\"QA Lead Application\\\", dashboard card fxwhkhvyli name = \\\"QA Lead Application\\\", and reopening the resume still shows that title in the editor header.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Customized section headings not rendered in every style: contact heading never rendered; summary heading missing in Minimal\", \"actual\": \"Renamed all 5 editable section titles to: Contact=\\\"How To Reach Me\\\", Summary=\\\"About Me\\\", Experience=\\\"Career History\\\", Education=\\\"Academic Background\\\", Skills=\\\"Core Competencies\\\". Modern preview shows About Me / Academic Background / Career History / Core Competencies but no \\\"How To Reach Me\\\"